<title>LITHUANIA: Yields edge down on 182-day Lithuanian T-bills.</title>
<headline>Yields edge down on 182-day Lithuanian T-bills.</headline>
<dateline>VILNIUS 1997-05-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Yields edged down on 182-day Lithuanian Treasury bills on Tuesday, the country's central bank said.</p>
<p>The average yield was 9.79 percent, down from the 9.83 percent offered at the last auction for 182-day paper on May 13.</p>
<p>The settlement date for the issue is May 23 and the bills mature on November 21.</p>
<p>All figures in millions of litas unless otherwise</p>
<p>indicated.</p>
<p>SOLD  DEMAND  MATURITY MIN/MAX YIELD  AV.YIELD  LAST AV.YIELD</p>
<p>50    98.679  182-DAYS   9.69/9.97	9.79	 9.83</p>
<p>-- Riga newsroom, +371 721 52 40</p>
